/E (Physically, Kenny relies more on agility, acceleration and movement than raw strength. At 1.78m, he is not an imposing attacker, but he has enough pace to attack defenders in wide areas and enough mobility to make repeated runs throughout matches.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (His game is built around receiving to feet, carrying the ball at opponents and attacking space. The dribbling numbers support the eye test, showing a player comfortable driving forward under pressure and progressing attacks individually. He is far more effective on the ground than in the air, with his aerial profile remaining a clear weakness.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (His durability is encouraging. Despite being only 20, he has handled regular Premier Division football, starting 16 league matches and consistently completing significant minutes. As he continues to mature physically, further gains in strength could make his direct style even more effective.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
